summary:
  A device that takes a command and never answers is reported in the words
  of whatever the socket raised, with nothing to tell it from a refusal.

history:
  The widget has to tell two things apart: a device that answered and
  turned the address down, and a device that could not be talked to. On
  2026-11-12 a Ruark that was sent an address it could not reach took the
  command and went silent until the helper's wait ran out. That is a
  timeout while SetAVTransportURI was asked, and the line says so in a
  field of its own.

target:
  package/contents/ui/cast.py

find:
      if isinstance(exc, Unreached):
          return "%s reach=%s action=%s" % (FAIL, exc.how, exc.action)

replace:
      if isinstance(exc, Unreached):
          return "%s %s" % (FAIL, exc)

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_cast_fault.py::test_a_device_that_takes_the_command_and_says_nothing_timed_out.
